================================================================================
libchdr - CHD v5 container: behaviour reference only, nothing copied
================================================================================

Source: https://github.com/rtissera/libchdr
License: BSD-3-Clause

Core/Formats/DiscImage/Chd/ reads MAME's CHD v5 container natively. It was written from the
format's behaviour as libchdr documents it - the header field order, the two-pass Huffman and
delta coding of the hunk map, the per-hunk CRC-16, the 'L'/'B' marker on a FLAC hunk and the
[ecc bitmap][sector data][subcode] framing of a CD hunk - together with the public LZMA
specification, RFC 9639 (FLAC) and ECMA-130 Annex A (CD-ROM ECC). No libchdr source was copied,
and MAME's own CHD sources (GPL-2.0-or-later) were never opened. chdman remains a separate
process where the corpus tooling needs it.

