================================================================================
Bink video (.bik) decoding - ORIGINAL WORK, NO THIRD-PARTY CODE
================================================================================

src/BethesdaMultitool/Core/Formats/Bink/ is an original clean-room implementation written for
this repository. It contains no code, and no transliteration of code, from FFmpeg, libav,
AweMultitool's FFmpeg-derived Bink files, or any other Bink implementation. It was produced
solely from:

  * our own reverse engineering of RAD Game Tools' shipped decoder binkw32.dll (as distributed
    with Fallout Tactics; md5 ecbd8213e89f8afde368f8eb05ff5a9c), through our own Ghidra
    decompilation and our own disassembly of that file;
  * the retail Bink bitstreams, read as data;
  * ffmpeg/ffprobe run as sealed executables, whose OUTPUT PIXELS were compared with ours. No
    FFmpeg source was read and no FFmpeg documentation of algorithm internals was consulted.

The numeric tables in BinkTables.cs (Huffman code books, scan orders, dequantisers, the
coefficient permutation) were extracted by us from binkw32.dll's .rdata at the virtual
addresses recorded in each table's comment. They are facts about a shipped binary, transcribed
for interoperability, not copied from any third party's source.

An earlier port of AweMultitool's Bink decoder (five files derived from FFmpeg's libavcodec
bink.c/binkdata.h/binkdsp.c, LGPL-2.1-or-later) was REMOVED from this repository on 2026-09-08
